    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** ERNIE-Image Turbo text to image (Baidu, 8B, Apache 2.0) in 8 steps, with the authors' optional prompt enhancer. Good at text in pictures, posters and layouts. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Prompt**: what the picture shows. Put text you want drawn in quotes.\n   - **Prompt enhancer**: true (template default) lets a small LLM rewrite your prompt into a long description first. False = your prompt is used as written (faster, closer to your words).\n   - **Size**: pick the shape; megapixels 1 = 1024x1024. Leave \"multiple\" at 16.\n   - **Steps**: 8, what the Turbo model is distilled for.\n   - **Seed**: fixed, so the first Run gives the README picture. Type a new number for a new picture.\n2. **Models**: the four loaders must show the files from the Downloads note.\n3. **Prompt enhancer**: nothing to change.\n4. **Prompt**: the preview node shows the prompt the model really gets (the enhanced one when the enhancer is on).\n5. **Sampling**: CFG 1, euler / simple, from the template. No negative prompt at CFG 1.\n6. Press **Run**. The picture is saved by the **Result** node to `output/ERNIE-Image/`.\n\n**What to expect:** 1024x1024 with the enhancer on: 29 s for the first Run in a 12 GiB VRAM budget (models loading, enhancer writing, 8 steps); 1360x768 with the enhancer off: 14 s. Measured on a 24 GB card, not a 12 GB one.\n**Tip:** for wide posters say \"wide landscape-format poster that fills the whole frame\". With only \"travel poster\" at 16:9 the model drew three tall posters side by side in 4 of 4 tries.\n\n**Tested on:** ComfyUI 0.45.3, RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB, VRAM capped with --reserve-vram to 12 GiB and 10 GiB (same pictures in both).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    -800,
    470
   ],
   "size": [
    640,
